# Pairs with RCommittedEventuallyVisible. A cross-tree receiver tree marks its
# registry with the barrier's verdict but never fans the terminal out to its
# leaves. Every read is still consistent - the registry's committed answer
# surfaces the pending buckets - so no safety property notices; only the
# liveness property does, because the committed write is never materialised.
MODULE: RCommittedEventuallyVisibleFinalizeSkipsFanOut
TARGET: RCommittedEventuallyVisible
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a finalised cross-tree receiver tree marks its registry but owes its leaves nothing
PERTURBS: ReceiverFinalize

--- FIND
    /\ rtodo' = rtodo \cup KeysOf(tr)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the finalise owes no fan-out.
    /\ rtodo' = rtodo
--- END
